WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.580
Hi, I'm Nei Maldaner,

2
00:00:01.580 --> 00:00:03.900
and this is track one of the

3
00:00:03.900 --> 00:00:05.740
LOOP-R course.

4
00:00:05.840 --> 00:00:07.640
This track is a diagnosis:

5
00:00:07.640 --> 00:00:09.560
why does your business use AI every

6
00:00:09.560 --> 00:00:11.200
day and still not improve?

7
00:00:11.200 --> 00:00:12.520
You will identify,

8
00:00:12.520 --> 00:00:13.740
in your own business,

9
00:00:13.740 --> 00:00:16.300
where AI does work but learns nothing.

10
00:00:16.300 --> 00:00:18.080
There are four lessons.

11
00:00:18.080 --> 00:00:19.080
In the first,

12
00:00:19.080 --> 00:00:20.200
you name the problem.

13
00:00:20.200 --> 00:00:21.100
In the second,

14
00:00:21.100 --> 00:00:22.680
you count the rework.

15
00:00:22.680 --> 00:00:23.680
In the third,

16
00:00:23.680 --> 00:00:25.320
you mark your maturity level,

17
00:00:25.320 --> 00:00:26.540
from one to five.

18
00:00:26.540 --> 00:00:27.600
In the fourth,

19
00:00:27.600 --> 00:00:30.000
you rewrite a vague instruction

20
00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:31.620
so its result can be measured.

21
00:00:31.620 --> 00:00:33.800
We will follow three people:

22
00:00:34.520 --> 00:00:36.980
Regina, who owns an aesthetics clinic;

23
00:00:36.980 --> 00:00:39.240
Marcos, a real estate agent;

24
00:00:39.240 --> 00:00:41.680
and Paulo, a support manager.

25
00:00:41.680 --> 00:00:43.920
Each lesson has a short practice.

26
00:00:43.920 --> 00:00:44.960
When I ask,

27
00:00:44.960 --> 00:00:46.860
pause the video and do it right

28
00:00:46.860 --> 00:00:48.540
then, using your own business.

29
00:00:48.540 --> 00:00:50.360
Today, in most businesses,

30
00:00:50.360 --> 00:00:52.740
AI works in a straight line.

31
00:00:52.740 --> 00:00:54.380
Someone writes a request,

32
00:00:54.380 --> 00:00:56.520
what people often call a prompt,

33
00:00:56.520 --> 00:00:58.840
AI replies, the

34
00:00:58.840 --> 00:01:00.860
person adjusts it and sends it.

35
00:01:00.860 --> 00:01:01.500
Done.

36
00:01:01.500 --> 00:01:02.700
Look at Regina.

37
00:01:02.700 --> 00:01:04.960
She sends about two hundred proposals a

38
00:01:04.960 --> 00:01:06.100
month over WhatsApp.

39
00:01:06.100 --> 00:01:08.520
She asks AI for a package proposal,

40
00:01:08.520 --> 00:01:09.740
changes two sentences,

41
00:01:09.740 --> 00:01:11.340
and sends it.

42
00:01:11.340 --> 00:01:14.640
The customer replies or disappears.

43
00:01:15.160 --> 00:01:17.220
Proposal number two hundred and one starts

44
00:01:17.220 --> 00:01:19.200
knowing nothing about the previous two hundred:

45
00:01:19.200 --> 00:01:20.500
not which got replies,

46
00:01:20.500 --> 00:01:22.040
or which led to a sale.

47
00:01:22.040 --> 00:01:23.040
Notice:

48
00:01:23.040 --> 00:01:25.040
every proposal was good.

49
00:01:25.040 --> 00:01:26.660
Quality is not the problem.

50
00:01:26.660 --> 00:01:28.900
The path has four stops and no

51
00:01:28.900 --> 00:01:29.760
way back.

52
00:01:29.760 --> 00:01:30.780
With a loop,

53
00:01:30.780 --> 00:01:33.260
those same two hundred proposals each become

54
00:01:33.260 --> 00:01:34.380
a row in a log,

55
00:01:34.380 --> 00:01:36.320
and one decision comes out each week

56
00:01:36.320 --> 00:01:37.560
on a five-line card.

57
00:01:37.560 --> 00:01:39.080
And that is not a flaw in

58
00:01:39.080 --> 00:01:39.580
AI.

59
00:01:39.520 --> 00:01:41.820
An AI chat is like an excellent

60
00:01:41.820 --> 00:01:45.040
temporary assistant who arrives new every shift.

61
00:01:45.040 --> 00:01:46.440
It writes very well,

62
00:01:46.440 --> 00:01:47.840
but it was not here yesterday.

63
00:01:47.840 --> 00:01:50.880
Everything that happens after the reply stays

64
00:01:50.880 --> 00:01:52.760
outside the conversation.

65
00:01:52.760 --> 00:01:54.360
Marcos, the real estate agent,

66
00:01:54.360 --> 00:01:56.480
gets about forty leads a week through

67
00:01:56.480 --> 00:01:57.860
the listing portal.

68
00:01:57.860 --> 00:01:59.180
A lead is someone who asked for

69
00:01:59.180 --> 00:02:01.160
information and has not decided yet.

70
00:02:01.160 --> 00:02:02.920
When a lead responds well because he

71
00:02:02.920 --> 00:02:04.440
mentioned the balcony’s square footage,

72
00:02:04.440 --> 00:02:05.740
that taught him something,

73
00:02:05.740 --> 00:02:07.400
if he noticed.

74
00:02:07.400 --> 00:02:09.680
To AI, the next lead is the

75
00:02:09.680 --> 00:02:10.960
first one it has ever seen.

76
00:02:10.960 --> 00:02:12.400
That is why using it a lot

77
00:02:12.400 --> 00:02:13.620
does not become learning.

78
00:02:13.620 --> 00:02:15.832
If Marcos used AI one hundred and

79
00:02:15.832 --> 00:02:17.560
sixty times this month,

80
00:02:17.560 --> 00:02:18.760
it

81
00:02:18.840 --> 00:02:21.940
knows nothing about what worked unless someone

82
00:02:21.940 --> 00:02:24.840
records the result and carries it forward.

83
00:02:24.840 --> 00:02:27.180
Real improvement does not come from asking

84
00:02:27.180 --> 00:02:27.680
better.

85
00:02:27.640 --> 00:02:30.160
It comes from six ingredients connected in

86
00:02:30.160 --> 00:02:31.440
a loop.

87
00:02:31.540 --> 00:02:33.360
Evidence: what happened,

88
00:02:33.360 --> 00:02:34.680
written down.

89
00:02:34.680 --> 00:02:37.280
Metric: a number that says whether it

90
00:02:37.280 --> 00:02:37.960
worked.

91
00:02:37.960 --> 00:02:41.120
Memory: where past attempts are kept.

92
00:02:41.120 --> 00:02:42.940
Hypothesis: an idea for a change,

93
00:02:42.940 --> 00:02:44.180
with a reason.

94
00:02:44.180 --> 00:02:45.100
Experiment:

95
00:02:45.100 --> 00:02:47.660
the idea tested against the current version.

96
00:02:47.660 --> 00:02:51.460
And evaluation: someone says which one won,

97
00:02:51.500 --> 00:02:53.180
based on the number.

98
00:02:53.180 --> 00:02:55.680
Paulo handles ten thousand support tickets a

99
00:02:55.680 --> 00:02:56.180
year.

100
00:02:56.180 --> 00:02:58.520
For him, the metric is resolved on

101
00:02:58.520 --> 00:03:00.680
first contact, yes or no.

102
00:03:00.680 --> 00:03:03.700
The hypothesis: if the password reply includes

103
00:03:03.700 --> 00:03:04.800
a direct link,

104
00:03:04.800 --> 00:03:07.080
fewer people will come back.

105
00:03:07.180 --> 00:03:09.780
The test: half the tickets get the

106
00:03:09.780 --> 00:03:11.920
new reply, half the old one.

107
00:03:11.920 --> 00:03:14.240
None of these six means asking more

108
00:03:14.240 --> 00:03:15.120
forcefully.

109
00:03:15.120 --> 00:03:16.240
If one is missing,

110
00:03:16.240 --> 00:03:17.760
the loop opens:

111
00:03:17.760 --> 00:03:20.600
a hypothesis without an experiment

112
00:03:20.600 --> 00:03:21.540
is a guess.

113
00:03:21.540 --> 00:03:22.880
Now, the anti-promise.

114
00:03:22.880 --> 00:03:24.580
No loop guarantees that the number will

115
00:03:24.580 --> 00:03:25.080
go up.

116
00:03:25.020 --> 00:03:27.980
The loop guarantees something more modest:

117
00:03:27.980 --> 00:03:30.640
a worse version does not replace the

118
00:03:30.640 --> 00:03:32.420
current one on its own.

119
00:03:32.420 --> 00:03:34.640
Every change is recorded and has a

120
00:03:34.640 --> 00:03:35.660
rollback button.

121
00:03:35.660 --> 00:03:37.780
The cycle runs every week.

122
00:03:37.780 --> 00:03:40.120
And the cost does not exceed the

123
00:03:40.120 --> 00:03:40.620
limit.

124
00:03:40.600 --> 00:03:41.740
This is process,

125
00:03:41.740 --> 00:03:43.440
not results.

126
00:03:43.480 --> 00:03:45.600
In the course reference example,

127
00:03:45.600 --> 00:03:48.640
a fictional clinic with simulated data,

128
00:03:48.640 --> 00:03:51.170
the proposal response rate went from nineteen

129
00:03:51.170 --> 00:03:53.660
point three to twenty-nine point three percent,

130
00:03:53.660 --> 00:03:54.695
with

131
00:03:54.695 --> 00:03:56.300
three hundred sends on each side.

132
00:03:56.300 --> 00:03:58.075
Sales conversion did not move:

133
00:03:58.075 --> 00:03:59.840
three point seven versus three percent,

134
00:03:59.840 --> 00:04:01.560
a difference that could be chance.

135
00:04:01.560 --> 00:04:03.560
The loop did not hide it.

136
00:04:03.560 --> 00:04:04.640
It recorded it,

137
00:04:04.640 --> 00:04:06.360
and the person decided with the numbers

138
00:04:06.360 --> 00:04:07.367
in front of them.

139
00:04:07.400 --> 00:04:09.080
Time to practice,

140
00:04:09.280 --> 00:04:10.960
about ten minutes.

141
00:04:10.960 --> 00:04:13.560
Regina uses AI for five things:

142
00:04:13.560 --> 00:04:14.880
proposals over WhatsApp,

143
00:04:14.880 --> 00:04:16.780
answering prices on Instagram,

144
00:04:16.780 --> 00:04:19.320
post captions, summaries of Google reviews,

145
00:04:19.320 --> 00:04:21.080
and appointment reminders.

146
00:04:21.080 --> 00:04:22.920
None records what happened afterward.

147
00:04:22.920 --> 00:04:24.800
And she thinks summarizing

148
00:04:24.800 --> 00:04:27.580
reviews already counts as learning.

149
00:04:27.580 --> 00:04:29.100
Pause the video and answer.

150
00:04:29.100 --> 00:04:30.920
Which of the five end there?

151
00:04:30.920 --> 00:04:32.280
Is task four a loop?

152
00:04:32.280 --> 00:04:34.320
Which would you choose to start tracking?

153
00:04:34.320 --> 00:04:36.480
According to the course answer key,

154
00:04:36.480 --> 00:04:37.920
all five end there.

155
00:04:37.920 --> 00:04:39.820
Reading reviews is not a loop,

156
00:04:39.820 --> 00:04:41.020
because

157
00:04:41.360 --> 00:04:43.020
reading is not learning;

158
00:04:43.020 --> 00:04:45.720
changing based on evidence is.

159
00:04:45.720 --> 00:04:47.700
The best choice is the proposal:

160
00:04:47.700 --> 00:04:48.980
it is the most frequent,

161
00:04:48.980 --> 00:04:51.500
and replies arrive within hours.

162
00:04:51.500 --> 00:04:54.040
Then write down five tasks in your

163
00:04:54.040 --> 00:04:55.600
business using this phrase:

164
00:04:55.600 --> 00:04:58.560
it ends there because nobody records such

165
00:04:58.560 --> 00:04:59.220
and such.

166
00:04:59.220 --> 00:05:00.440
Second lesson.

167
00:05:00.440 --> 00:05:02.667
Volume creates a feeling of experience.

168
00:05:02.667 --> 00:05:05.040
Ten thousand tickets sound like ten thousand

169
00:05:05.040 --> 00:05:05.560
lessons.

170
00:05:05.560 --> 00:05:07.500
But if nobody wrote down what they

171
00:05:07.500 --> 00:05:09.700
were about, those ten thousand are worth

172
00:05:09.700 --> 00:05:11.680
as much as the first one.

173
00:05:11.680 --> 00:05:13.360
Paulo ends the year with ten thousand

174
00:05:13.360 --> 00:05:14.880
tickets, each resolved well.

175
00:05:14.880 --> 00:05:16.920
And nobody knows that thirty-seven percent of

176
00:05:16.920 --> 00:05:18.560
them, three thousand seven hundred,

177
00:05:18.560 --> 00:05:20.320
concern the same problem:

178
00:05:20.320 --> 00:05:23.760
a password screen that confuses everyone.

179
00:05:23.760 --> 00:05:25.340
Why did nobody notice?

180
00:05:25.340 --> 00:05:26.780
From inside one ticket,

181
00:05:26.780 --> 00:05:27.980
you cannot see the pile.

182
00:05:27.980 --> 00:05:29.760
Only someone looking at the whole set,

183
00:05:29.760 --> 00:05:31.500
with a topic column filled in,

184
00:05:31.500 --> 00:05:33.360
sees that one in three points to

185
00:05:33.360 --> 00:05:34.860
the same thing.

186
00:05:35.140 --> 00:05:36.060
Those

187
00:05:36.060 --> 00:05:38.840
ten thousand produced zero product changes.

188
00:05:38.840 --> 00:05:41.020
One fix to that screen would have

189
00:05:41.020 --> 00:05:43.760
prevented three thousand seven hundred conversations.

190
00:05:44.520 --> 00:05:47.260
Starting from scratch has a cost that

191
00:05:47.260 --> 00:05:49.400
does not appear on the invoice.

192
00:05:49.400 --> 00:05:51.676
Marcos replies to about one hundred and

193
00:05:51.676 --> 00:05:53.000
sixty leads a month.

194
00:05:53.000 --> 00:05:55.080
Each reply takes about six minutes to

195
00:05:55.080 --> 00:05:57.440
request, adjust, and send.

196
00:05:57.440 --> 00:05:59.960
That is sixteen hours a month.

197
00:05:59.960 --> 00:06:02.240
And next month’s hours will buy the

198
00:06:02.240 --> 00:06:04.480
same thing: one hundred and sixty isolated

199
00:06:04.480 --> 00:06:05.620
replies.

200
00:06:05.620 --> 00:06:06.700
Now compare.

201
00:06:06.700 --> 00:06:07.680
The same time,

202
00:06:07.680 --> 00:06:08.700
the

203
00:06:08.700 --> 00:06:11.500
same replies, but each leaves a row:

204
00:06:11.500 --> 00:06:13.320
date, property type,

205
00:06:13.320 --> 00:06:16.040
opening used, whether the lead replied,

206
00:06:16.040 --> 00:06:17.700
whether they booked a viewing.

207
00:06:17.700 --> 00:06:19.340
The effort is the same.

208
00:06:19.340 --> 00:06:20.860
The difference is the trail.

209
00:06:20.860 --> 00:06:21.980
In one case,

210
00:06:21.980 --> 00:06:23.820
all that remains is fatigue.

211
00:06:23.820 --> 00:06:24.780
In the other,

212
00:06:24.780 --> 00:06:26.560
there is material for a question Marcos

213
00:06:26.560 --> 00:06:28.040
cannot answer today:

214
00:06:28.040 --> 00:06:30.940
which opening gets more people to book?

215
00:06:30.940 --> 00:06:33.440
Today everyone has access to the same

216
00:06:33.440 --> 00:06:34.380
AI,

217
00:06:34.380 --> 00:06:35.620
equally capable.

218
00:06:35.620 --> 00:06:39.160
Think of two real estate agencies with

219
00:06:39.580 --> 00:06:40.420
the same chat,

220
00:06:40.420 --> 00:06:41.620
the same portals,

221
00:06:41.620 --> 00:06:43.280
and the same neighborhood.

222
00:06:43.280 --> 00:06:44.920
What separates them?

223
00:06:44.920 --> 00:06:46.810
It is not the

224
00:06:46.810 --> 00:06:47.460
better-written request.

225
00:06:47.460 --> 00:06:48.400
That

226
00:06:48.400 --> 00:06:49.740
can be copied in a day.

227
00:06:49.740 --> 00:06:52.200
What cannot be copied is the history.

228
00:06:52.200 --> 00:06:54.400
One records, for

229
00:06:54.840 --> 00:06:56.720
each lead, the channel,

230
00:06:56.720 --> 00:06:59.200
property type, reply sent,

231
00:06:59.200 --> 00:07:00.740
and what happened.

232
00:07:00.740 --> 00:07:02.100
After six months,

233
00:07:02.100 --> 00:07:03.820
it has about a thousand rows to

234
00:07:03.820 --> 00:07:05.800
consult before changing anything.

235
00:07:05.800 --> 00:07:08.200
The other has a thousand lost conversations

236
00:07:08.200 --> 00:07:09.920
in each agent’s WhatsApp.

237
00:07:09.920 --> 00:07:11.700
A competitor can copy the text.

238
00:07:11.700 --> 00:07:13.460
They cannot copy six months of what

239
00:07:13.460 --> 00:07:15.460
we tested and how it went.

240
00:07:15.460 --> 00:07:18.100
That accumulated history is the asset,

241
00:07:18.100 --> 00:07:19.920
and it begins with one row per

242
00:07:19.920 --> 00:07:20.960
run, every day.

243
00:07:20.960 --> 00:07:21.920
The

244
00:07:21.920 --> 00:07:24.160
whole loop depends on one humble step:

245
00:07:24.160 --> 00:07:24.860
logging.

246
00:07:24.860 --> 00:07:26.740
The place is the logging spreadsheet:

247
00:07:26.740 --> 00:07:29.040
one row per run and a column

248
00:07:29.040 --> 00:07:30.140
most people forget,

249
00:07:30.140 --> 00:07:32.080
what happened afterward.

250
00:07:32.080 --> 00:07:34.000
Without it, you have a file of

251
00:07:34.000 --> 00:07:35.820
texts, not evidence.

252
00:07:35.820 --> 00:07:37.100
In Paulo’s support team,

253
00:07:37.100 --> 00:07:39.060
there are five columns:

254
00:07:39.060 --> 00:07:40.940
date, ticket

255
00:07:40.940 --> 00:07:43.080
topic, saved reply used,

256
00:07:43.080 --> 00:07:44.420
resolved on first contact,

257
00:07:44.420 --> 00:07:45.360
and

258
00:07:45.360 --> 00:07:47.300
came back within seven days.

259
00:07:47.300 --> 00:07:49.360
The question about what people complain about

260
00:07:49.360 --> 00:07:51.400
most, which took a week of reading,

261
00:07:51.400 --> 00:07:52.880
becomes a two-minute count.

262
00:07:52.880 --> 00:07:54.960
Two honest points about the method.

263
00:07:54.960 --> 00:07:56.940
The evidence source is the bottleneck,

264
00:07:56.940 --> 00:07:59.040
not AI: if the data live in

265
00:07:59.040 --> 00:08:00.080
the salesperson’s head,

266
00:08:00.080 --> 00:08:02.160
the loop becomes theater.

267
00:08:02.160 --> 00:08:04.160
And twelve rows do not make a

268
00:08:04.160 --> 00:08:04.660
pattern.

269
00:08:04.600 --> 00:08:06.100
The loop’s rule is to claim a

270
00:08:06.100 --> 00:08:08.040
pattern only with thirty or more per

271
00:08:08.040 --> 00:08:08.600
group.

272
00:08:08.600 --> 00:08:09.660
Now the practice,

273
00:08:09.660 --> 00:08:11.460
about ten minutes.

274
00:08:11.460 --> 00:08:12.800
This is just counting;

275
00:08:12.800 --> 00:08:14.760
nothing changes in your business.

276
00:08:14.760 --> 00:08:15.900
Pause the video.

277
00:08:15.900 --> 00:08:17.820
Choose a task AI does for you

278
00:08:17.820 --> 00:08:18.540
every week.

279
00:08:18.540 --> 00:08:20.360
Open WhatsApp, email,

280
00:08:20.360 --> 00:08:22.320
or the system from last month and

281
00:08:22.320 --> 00:08:23.800
count how many times it happened.

282
00:08:23.800 --> 00:08:25.640
If counting all of them feels like

283
00:08:25.640 --> 00:08:28.340
too much, estimate one week and multiply

284
00:08:28.340 --> 00:08:29.320
by four.

285
00:08:29.320 --> 00:08:30.400
For each one,

286
00:08:30.400 --> 00:08:31.380
ask:

287
00:08:31.380 --> 00:08:33.800
do I know what happened afterward?

288
00:08:33.800 --> 00:08:35.700
Count the ones where the answer is

289
00:08:35.700 --> 00:08:36.300
no.

290
00:08:36.300 --> 00:08:38.700
Then write a sentence with two numbers.

291
00:08:38.700 --> 00:08:41.516
For example: replies to portal leads,

292
00:08:41.516 --> 00:08:43.516
one hundred and sixty times a month,

293
00:08:43.516 --> 00:08:45.280
one hundred and sixty without

294
00:08:45.280 --> 00:08:46.480
a record.

295
00:08:46.480 --> 00:08:48.500
Then, in the next fifteen minutes,

296
00:08:48.500 --> 00:08:50.640
create a spreadsheet with five columns:

297
00:08:50.640 --> 00:08:52.140
date, what was sent,

298
00:08:52.140 --> 00:08:53.520
to whom, what happened,

299
00:08:53.520 --> 00:08:54.360
and notes.

300
00:08:54.360 --> 00:08:57.360
Fill in the last three times.

301
00:08:57.840 --> 00:08:58.940
Third lesson.

302
00:08:58.940 --> 00:09:01.280
Everyone who uses AI thinks they are

303
00:09:01.280 --> 00:09:03.870
advanced, and almost everyone is at level

304
00:09:03.870 --> 00:09:04.370
one.

305
00:09:04.020 --> 00:09:05.760
Without a yardstick,

306
00:09:05.760 --> 00:09:07.840
you buy a level-four tool for a

307
00:09:07.840 --> 00:09:08.700
level-one problem.

308
00:09:08.700 --> 00:09:09.540
At level one,

309
00:09:09.540 --> 00:09:10.960
AI responds:

310
00:09:11.200 --> 00:09:13.200
you write, it delivers,

311
00:09:13.200 --> 00:09:15.060
you check and use it.

312
00:09:15.060 --> 00:09:17.260
The intelligence lives in your head.

313
00:09:17.260 --> 00:09:18.640
Regina is here.

314
00:09:18.640 --> 00:09:19.980
Level one is not bad:

315
00:09:19.980 --> 00:09:21.800
getting a good reply a thousand times

316
00:09:21.800 --> 00:09:23.000
saves many hours.

317
00:09:23.000 --> 00:09:24.300
It just is not learning.

318
00:09:24.300 --> 00:09:25.320
At level two,

319
00:09:25.320 --> 00:09:27.380
an assistant with one job comes in.

320
00:09:27.380 --> 00:09:28.580
You give it a goal,

321
00:09:28.580 --> 00:09:30.300
it plans, uses a tool,

322
00:09:30.300 --> 00:09:31.840
and delivers.

323
00:09:31.910 --> 00:09:32.920
Marcos’s

324
00:09:32.920 --> 00:09:34.440
assistant reads the lead,

325
00:09:34.440 --> 00:09:36.340
finds the property in the spreadsheet,

326
00:09:36.340 --> 00:09:37.160
writes the reply,

327
00:09:37.160 --> 00:09:39.580
and suggests two viewing times.

328
00:09:39.580 --> 00:09:40.360
It does more,

329
00:09:40.360 --> 00:09:41.460
and

330
00:09:41.460 --> 00:09:42.700
learns just as much:

331
00:09:42.700 --> 00:09:43.380
nothing.

332
00:09:43.380 --> 00:09:46.520
Nobody records whether the viewing happened.

333
00:09:46.520 --> 00:09:47.660
At level three,

334
00:09:47.660 --> 00:09:49.180
the business learns.

335
00:09:49.180 --> 00:09:50.820
Each run becomes a row,

336
00:09:50.820 --> 00:09:53.420
and every week someone proposes a hypothesis,

337
00:09:53.420 --> 00:09:55.440
tests the new version against the current

338
00:09:55.440 --> 00:09:57.240
one, and decides by the number.

339
00:09:57.240 --> 00:09:59.340
In the course reference example,

340
00:09:59.340 --> 00:10:01.060
using simulated data,

341
00:10:01.060 --> 00:10:02.540
the loop ran four cycles.

342
00:10:02.540 --> 00:10:06.160
The hypothesis to open by mentioning the

343
00:10:06.280 --> 00:10:09.280
customer’s review, tested with three hundred proposals

344
00:10:09.280 --> 00:10:10.440
on each side,

345
00:10:10.440 --> 00:10:13.596
raised replies from nineteen point three to

346
00:10:13.596 --> 00:10:14.620
twenty-nine point three percent,

347
00:10:14.620 --> 00:10:17.700
without worsening what was being monitored,

348
00:10:17.700 --> 00:10:18.960
so it was promoted.

349
00:10:18.960 --> 00:10:21.460
Another version, up to eighty words,

350
00:10:21.460 --> 00:10:23.700
rose almost as much and was rejected

351
00:10:23.700 --> 00:10:24.780
by a rule.

352
00:10:24.780 --> 00:10:26.593
There are three degrees of autonomy.

353
00:10:26.593 --> 00:10:28.673
L zero only suggests.

354
00:10:28.673 --> 00:10:31.620
L one: you approve each change on

355
00:10:31.620 --> 00:10:32.780
a five-line card.

356
00:10:32.780 --> 00:10:35.370
L two promotes on its own after

357
00:10:35.370 --> 00:10:37.220
five correct approvals from you.

358
00:10:37.220 --> 00:10:39.467
The course builds yours at

359
00:10:39.467 --> 00:10:40.520
L one.

360
00:10:40.520 --> 00:10:42.920
Level four is a system that observes

361
00:10:42.920 --> 00:10:44.380
its own improvement system:

362
00:10:44.380 --> 00:10:46.000
how much each cycle costs,

363
00:10:46.000 --> 00:10:48.480
and how many hypotheses became versions.

364
00:10:48.480 --> 00:10:49.660
In the product today,

365
00:10:49.660 --> 00:10:51.560
this level only reports.

366
00:10:51.560 --> 00:10:53.940
It does not redesign anything on its

367
00:10:53.940 --> 00:10:56.520
own, because a system that changes itself

368
00:10:56.520 --> 00:10:58.660
with little data multiplies

369
00:10:58.680 --> 00:11:00.120
every error.

370
00:11:00.120 --> 00:11:01.600
This is still research.

371
00:11:01.600 --> 00:11:03.340
Level five is the whole business,

372
00:11:03.340 --> 00:11:05.580
every department with its own loop.

373
00:11:05.580 --> 00:11:07.020
In Paulo’s support team:

374
00:11:07.020 --> 00:11:08.580
tickets are logged,

375
00:11:08.580 --> 00:11:09.780
the cause is found in the password

376
00:11:09.780 --> 00:11:11.860
screen, a new reply is tested,

377
00:11:11.860 --> 00:11:13.440
and a change is suggested to the

378
00:11:13.440 --> 00:11:13.960
product.

379
00:11:13.960 --> 00:11:16.080
But that only exists because every ticket

380
00:11:16.080 --> 00:11:17.000
became a row.

381
00:11:17.000 --> 00:11:18.220
So here is the rule:

382
00:11:18.220 --> 00:11:19.540
you cannot skip a level.

383
00:11:19.540 --> 00:11:20.440
If

384
00:11:20.440 --> 00:11:22.040
you are at one and buy level

385
00:11:22.040 --> 00:11:23.400
five, you are buying theater.

386
00:11:23.400 --> 00:11:26.080
The useful next step is level three,

387
00:11:26.080 --> 00:11:28.520
starting with one more column and a

388
00:11:28.520 --> 00:11:29.940
test with a number.

389
00:11:30.000 --> 00:11:32.460
Lesson practice, about twelve minutes.

390
00:11:32.460 --> 00:11:35.380
Pause and mark each person’s level.

391
00:11:35.640 --> 00:11:38.260
Regina requests each proposal and edits it

392
00:11:38.260 --> 00:11:39.340
by hand.

393
00:11:39.340 --> 00:11:41.440
Marcos has an assistant that suggests a

394
00:11:41.440 --> 00:11:42.360
viewing on its own,

395
00:11:42.360 --> 00:11:44.960
without anyone recording whether it happened.

396
00:11:44.960 --> 00:11:46.420
Paulo logs each ticket,

397
00:11:46.420 --> 00:11:48.260
tests a new reply against the old

398
00:11:48.260 --> 00:11:49.160
one every month,

399
00:11:49.160 --> 00:11:51.160
and decides on a card.

400
00:11:51.160 --> 00:11:53.210
According to the answer key:

401
00:11:53.210 --> 00:11:54.900
Regina, level one.

402
00:11:54.900 --> 00:11:56.500
Marcos, level two.

403
00:11:56.500 --> 00:11:57.880
Paulo, level three.

404
00:11:57.880 --> 00:11:58.860
Regina

405
00:11:58.860 --> 00:12:00.400
and Marcos need the same step:

406
00:12:00.400 --> 00:12:01.940
a results column.

407
00:12:01.940 --> 00:12:03.720
Now look

408
00:12:03.740 --> 00:12:04.560
at your business.

409
00:12:04.560 --> 00:12:06.500
Is there a row for every run?

410
00:12:06.500 --> 00:12:08.820
Has there been a test with numbers?

411
00:12:08.820 --> 00:12:10.660
Is a decision recorded?

412
00:12:10.660 --> 00:12:13.080
If you are unsure between two levels,

413
00:12:13.080 --> 00:12:14.750
mark the lower one.

414
00:12:14.750 --> 00:12:17.100
Write: I am at this level because

415
00:12:17.100 --> 00:12:17.880
of this sign,

416
00:12:17.880 --> 00:12:20.060
and my next step is this.

417
00:12:20.060 --> 00:12:22.280
Send that three-line message to your business

418
00:12:22.280 --> 00:12:23.340
partner.

419
00:12:23.340 --> 00:12:26.840
Fourth lesson: the mistake that sounds smart.

420
00:12:26.840 --> 00:12:29.820
Paulo wrote this in the support assistant:

421
00:12:29.820 --> 00:12:32.100
analyze your replies and keep improving.

422
00:12:32.100 --> 00:12:33.120
A month later,

423
00:12:33.120 --> 00:12:34.560
the assistant said yes,

424
00:12:34.560 --> 00:12:35.600
it had improved.

425
00:12:35.600 --> 00:12:37.280
And there

426
00:12:37.360 --> 00:12:38.730
was no way to know.

427
00:12:38.730 --> 00:12:41.380
The sentence creates the feeling of improvement

428
00:12:41.380 --> 00:12:43.960
without producing improvement.

429
00:12:43.960 --> 00:12:45.620
Three questions are missing.

430
00:12:45.620 --> 00:12:47.980
Improve compared with what?

431
00:12:47.980 --> 00:12:49.100
Measured by whom?

432
00:12:49.100 --> 00:12:51.280
Compared how, against what,

433
00:12:51.280 --> 00:12:53.080
and across how many cases?

434
00:12:53.080 --> 00:12:54.900
This is not an AI limitation;

435
00:12:54.900 --> 00:12:56.960
it is a problem with the request.

436
00:12:56.960 --> 00:12:58.960
That is why the course has an

437
00:12:58.960 --> 00:13:01.080
anchor sentence: do not ask AI to

438
00:13:01.080 --> 00:13:01.640
improve.

439
00:13:01.640 --> 00:13:03.760
Make every run produce evidence,

440
00:13:03.760 --> 00:13:06.560
every piece of evidence generate a hypothesis,

441
00:13:06.560 --> 00:13:08.820
every hypothesis become an experiment,

442
00:13:08.820 --> 00:13:10.920
and only what is proven enters the

443
00:13:10.920 --> 00:13:11.640
next version.

444
00:13:11.640 --> 00:13:13.640
The first change is to replace “improve”

445
00:13:13.640 --> 00:13:15.040
with “from X to Y,

446
00:13:15.040 --> 00:13:17.600
without worsening Z.” For Regina:

447
00:13:17.600 --> 00:13:20.560
proposal response rate from twenty to thirty

448
00:13:20.560 --> 00:13:24.700
percent, without worsening complaints or average discount.

449
00:13:24.760 --> 00:13:27.000
“Without worsening” has a name:

450
00:13:27.000 --> 00:13:28.240
a guardrail.

451
00:13:28.240 --> 00:13:30.740
Without it, every goal becomes a target,

452
00:13:30.740 --> 00:13:32.940
and the assistant learns to cheat.

453
00:13:32.940 --> 00:13:35.640
Ask for less time per ticket and

454
00:13:35.700 --> 00:13:37.960
the team closes it without resolving it.

455
00:13:37.960 --> 00:13:39.860
The number goes up and the business

456
00:13:39.860 --> 00:13:40.720
gets worse.

457
00:13:40.720 --> 00:13:41.840
Two cautions.

458
00:13:41.840 --> 00:13:43.140
Choose a fast metric,

459
00:13:43.140 --> 00:13:44.360
such as replies,

460
00:13:44.360 --> 00:13:46.060
and watch the money metric as a

461
00:13:46.060 --> 00:13:46.620
guardrail.

462
00:13:46.620 --> 00:13:48.840
And avoid goals near

463
00:13:49.313 --> 00:13:49.820
three percent.

464
00:13:49.820 --> 00:13:50.880
Proving

465
00:13:50.880 --> 00:13:53.000
a change from three to five takes

466
00:13:53.000 --> 00:13:55.180
about one thousand five hundred runs on

467
00:13:55.180 --> 00:13:57.490
each side: at two hundred a month,

468
00:13:57.490 --> 00:13:58.500
fifteen months.

469
00:13:58.500 --> 00:14:01.660
From twenty to thirty takes about three

470
00:14:01.660 --> 00:14:02.160
hundred.

471
00:14:01.960 --> 00:14:03.620
Start where you can prove it.

472
00:14:03.620 --> 00:14:05.780
The second change is

473
00:14:05.820 --> 00:14:08.000
to turn an idea into a hypothesis

474
00:14:08.000 --> 00:14:09.520
with a fixed form:

475
00:14:09.520 --> 00:14:11.080
if one change,

476
00:14:11.080 --> 00:14:13.120
then an effect on the goal,

477
00:14:13.120 --> 00:14:14.580
because of one reason.

478
00:14:14.580 --> 00:14:15.780
Regina would write:

479
00:14:15.780 --> 00:14:18.040
if the proposal opens by mentioning the

480
00:14:18.040 --> 00:14:19.620
review the customer left,

481
00:14:19.620 --> 00:14:21.960
then more customers will reply,

482
00:14:21.960 --> 00:14:24.900
because they recognize the message was written

483
00:14:24.900 --> 00:14:25.680
for them.

484
00:14:25.680 --> 00:14:27.720
And make one change only.

485
00:14:27.720 --> 00:14:29.620
Marcos wants to shorten the text,

486
00:14:29.620 --> 00:14:30.560
change the tone,

487
00:14:30.560 --> 00:14:32.200
and send it in the morning,

488
00:14:32.200 --> 00:14:33.340
all at once.

489
00:14:33.340 --> 00:14:34.420
If it works,

490
00:14:34.420 --> 00:14:35.800
he will not know which of the

491
00:14:35.800 --> 00:14:36.600
three worked.

492
00:14:36.600 --> 00:14:39.520
Look at Paulo’s request after the changes.

493
00:14:39.520 --> 00:14:40.720
Goal:

494
00:14:40.820 --> 00:14:43.500
resolved on first contact from fifty to

495
00:14:43.500 --> 00:14:47.540
sixty-five percent, without worsening seven-day reopenings.

496
00:14:47.780 --> 00:14:50.340
Hypothesis: a direct link in the password

497
00:14:50.340 --> 00:14:51.340
reply.

498
00:14:51.340 --> 00:14:52.300
Test:

499
00:14:52.300 --> 00:14:53.800
half get each version,

500
00:14:53.800 --> 00:14:56.180
about one hundred and seventy per version.

501
00:14:56.280 --> 00:14:58.280
The third change is to separate the

502
00:14:58.280 --> 00:15:00.500
person who proposes from the person who

503
00:15:00.500 --> 00:15:01.320
judges.

504
00:15:01.320 --> 00:15:04.020
The judge has only three answers.

505
00:15:04.340 --> 00:15:06.120
B won by a margin.

506
00:15:06.120 --> 00:15:07.980
A stays.

507
00:15:08.100 --> 00:15:09.900
Or not enough data:

508
00:15:09.900 --> 00:15:11.400
continue the test.

509
00:15:11.400 --> 00:15:12.860
That is the most common answer,

510
00:15:12.860 --> 00:15:14.453
and it has to be acceptable.

511
00:15:14.453 --> 00:15:16.620
Three hundred on each side is the

512
00:15:16.620 --> 00:15:17.740
amount needed for proof,

513
00:15:17.740 --> 00:15:19.660
calculated before the test.

514
00:15:19.660 --> 00:15:21.560
Here is the second quiet mistake:

515
00:15:21.560 --> 00:15:23.980
stopping the test halfway because the new

516
00:15:23.980 --> 00:15:25.150
version is ahead.

517
00:15:25.150 --> 00:15:26.980
Marcos, with forty leads a week,

518
00:15:26.980 --> 00:15:28.180
needs

519
00:15:28.180 --> 00:15:30.460
about fifteen weeks to reach three hundred

520
00:15:30.460 --> 00:15:31.700
per version.

521
00:15:31.700 --> 00:15:32.840
In week two,

522
00:15:32.840 --> 00:15:34.780
the new one has twelve replies out

523
00:15:34.780 --> 00:15:37.380
of forty, versus seven out of forty

524
00:15:37.380 --> 00:15:38.560
for the old one.

525
00:15:38.560 --> 00:15:39.920
He wants to promote it.

526
00:15:39.920 --> 00:15:42.060
But that can appear and disappear on

527
00:15:42.060 --> 00:15:42.760
its own.

528
00:15:42.760 --> 00:15:45.480
The right answer is not enough data.

529
00:15:45.480 --> 00:15:47.760
Only a falling guardrail justifies

530
00:15:47.760 --> 00:15:48.560
stopping early.

531
00:15:48.560 --> 00:15:50.300
Back to the reference example.

532
00:15:50.300 --> 00:15:51.180
In cycle two,

533
00:15:51.180 --> 00:15:53.460
the hypothesis of up to eighty words

534
00:15:53.460 --> 00:15:56.337
raised replies from nineteen point three to

535
00:15:56.337 --> 00:15:57.763
twenty-nine point seven percent.

536
00:15:57.763 --> 00:15:59.900
Ten points, with enough cases to prove

537
00:15:59.900 --> 00:16:00.500
it.

538
00:16:00.500 --> 00:16:02.140
And it was not promoted.

539
00:16:02.140 --> 00:16:05.200
The complaints guardrail showed six versus one,

540
00:16:05.200 --> 00:16:07.400
and the agreed tolerance was zero.

541
00:16:07.400 --> 00:16:08.960
The rule was applied.

542
00:16:08.960 --> 00:16:11.370
But it was poorly calibrated:

543
00:16:11.370 --> 00:16:13.020
six versus one out of three hundred

544
00:16:13.020 --> 00:16:14.060
is noise.

545
00:16:14.060 --> 00:16:16.387
The person adjusted the tolerance to one

546
00:16:16.387 --> 00:16:17.660
percent in later tests,

547
00:16:17.660 --> 00:16:19.900
and the hypothesis stayed in memory with

548
00:16:19.900 --> 00:16:20.540
the reason.

549
00:16:20.540 --> 00:16:21.600
In cycle four,

550
00:16:21.600 --> 00:16:24.270
mentioning the review raised replies to twenty-nine

551
00:16:24.270 --> 00:16:26.800
point three, the guardrails stayed within bounds,

552
00:16:26.800 --> 00:16:28.460
and it became official.

553
00:16:28.460 --> 00:16:31.120
The common mistake is promoting it because

554
00:16:31.120 --> 00:16:32.300
it looks better.

555
00:16:32.300 --> 00:16:32.980
At L one,

556
00:16:32.980 --> 00:16:34.740
you are the one who approves it,

557
00:16:34.740 --> 00:16:36.440
on the card.

558
00:16:36.740 --> 00:16:38.940
Last practice, about ten minutes,

559
00:16:38.940 --> 00:16:40.460
in any AI chat.

560
00:16:40.460 --> 00:16:42.920
The course provides a ready-made request to

561
00:16:42.920 --> 00:16:43.820
paste.

562
00:16:43.820 --> 00:16:45.200
You replace three parts:

563
00:16:45.200 --> 00:16:47.280
the task, the

564
00:16:47.280 --> 00:16:49.560
vague instruction, and the current number,

565
00:16:49.560 --> 00:16:52.340
or “I don’t know.” The request asks

566
00:16:52.340 --> 00:16:53.340
for four parts,

567
00:16:53.340 --> 00:16:55.660
without inventing numbers.

568
00:16:55.660 --> 00:16:57.200
Evidence: what to record,

569
00:16:57.200 --> 00:16:58.940
in up to five columns,

570
00:16:58.940 --> 00:17:01.020
one of them what happened afterward.

571
00:17:01.020 --> 00:17:03.620
Goal: from X to

572
00:17:03.620 --> 00:17:06.000
Y, without worsening Z.

573
00:17:06.000 --> 00:17:08.020
Hypothesis: if, then,

574
00:17:08.020 --> 00:17:10.300
because, with one change only.

575
00:17:10.300 --> 00:17:12.800
Test: two versions and how many runs

576
00:17:12.800 --> 00:17:13.540
per version.

577
00:17:13.540 --> 00:17:14.560
And at the end,

578
00:17:14.560 --> 00:17:16.860
what cannot change without your approval.

579
00:17:16.860 --> 00:17:18.160
Pause and do it.

580
00:17:18.160 --> 00:17:20.920
If the hypothesis includes several changes,

581
00:17:20.920 --> 00:17:22.480
ask to separate them.

582
00:17:22.480 --> 00:17:23.800
Save the text:

583
00:17:23.800 --> 00:17:25.760
it is the first draft of your

584
00:17:25.760 --> 00:17:26.540
loop worksheet.

585
00:17:26.540 --> 00:17:28.980
Then check the goal by counting the

586
00:17:28.980 --> 00:17:30.300
last twenty runs.

587
00:17:30.300 --> 00:17:31.980
Let’s bring it all together.

588
00:17:31.980 --> 00:17:34.180
Today, AI works in a straight line:

589
00:17:34.180 --> 00:17:36.220
someone asks, it replies,

590
00:17:36.220 --> 00:17:37.000
done.

591
00:17:37.000 --> 00:17:38.300
That is not its flaw;

592
00:17:38.300 --> 00:17:39.880
what is missing is a record of

593
00:17:39.880 --> 00:17:41.020
what happened afterward.

594
00:17:41.020 --> 00:17:43.820
Volume without records is not experience,

595
00:17:43.820 --> 00:17:46.060
and with the same AI available to

596
00:17:46.060 --> 00:17:48.660
everyone, history is what cannot be copied.

597
00:17:48.660 --> 00:17:50.680
You marked your level using signs;

598
00:17:50.680 --> 00:17:52.660
the useful next step is level three,

599
00:17:52.660 --> 00:17:53.600
at L one.

600
00:17:53.600 --> 00:17:56.400
And you replaced “get better” with evidence,

601
00:17:56.400 --> 00:17:58.700
a goal with “without worsening,”

602
00:17:58.840 --> 00:18:00.040
a

603
00:18:00.420 --> 00:18:02.620
hypothesis with one change only,

604
00:18:02.620 --> 00:18:04.920
and a test with enough cases to

605
00:18:04.920 --> 00:18:05.440
prove it.

606
00:18:05.440 --> 00:18:08.020
The loop does not guarantee the number

607
00:18:08.020 --> 00:18:09.240
will go up;

608
00:18:09.240 --> 00:18:11.620
it guarantees that a worse version does

609
00:18:11.620 --> 00:18:13.160
not enter on its own.

610
00:18:13.160 --> 00:18:14.040
In track two,

611
00:18:14.040 --> 00:18:15.200
you will build L,

612
00:18:15.200 --> 00:18:17.300
O, O, P,

613
00:18:17.300 --> 00:18:19.260
R step by step,

614
00:18:19.260 --> 00:18:20.540
starting with L,

615
00:18:20.540 --> 00:18:22.120
Locate: one process,

616
00:18:22.120 --> 00:18:22.840
one number.

617
00:18:22.840 --> 00:18:23.680
See you then.
